;; GNU-verified. Notable: `insert` does NOT inherit text properties
;; (only insert-and-inherit does); overlays-at covers beg<=pos<end and
;; sorts by descending priority; overlays-in sorts by descending
;; overlay-start (ascending end on ties); get-pos-property on a buffer
;; uses "char before pos" rear-sticky semantics; buffer-has-markers-at
;; and insert-string are void in GNU 31.1 (skipped).

